From 7171bb46f13eebf6901c6a4822383a5d0143873f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orlfman <25542856+orlfman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:31:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] linux: add AMD GPU usage, VRAM and power meters

Add three header meters for the RX 9070 XT, fed by the AMDGPU sampler:
AMDGPUUsage (caption "GPU") shows the GPU busy percentage, AMDGPUVRAM
("VRM") the used and total video memory, and AMDGPUPower ("Pwr") the
power draw against the power limit. They follow SwapMeter's layout: one
value against a total in bar and graph mode, and the values after the
caption in text mode.

The VRAM caption is "VRM" since bar and graph modes only draw the first
three characters of a caption. A value that is not available shows
"N/A", and a runtime suspended card shows "sleep". Existing colors are
reused, so the color schemes stay untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
